<body>
    <h1>Manual Removal of AI+ Installer</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h3 id=3D"ManualRemovalofAI+Installer-Currently,thereisnoone-clicko=
rofficialwaytoremovetheAI+installeralongwithitsinstallationdataandtheAI+Adm=
in.">Currently, there is <strong>no one-click or official way</strong> to r=
emove the AI+ installer along with its installation data and the AI+ Admin.=
</h3>
<p>To <strong>completely wipe AI+ Admin</strong> and all its related servic=
es, containers, and configurations from your system, follow the steps below=
 <strong>carefully</strong>.</p>
<p>This guide assumes, you are having a server where you are only running s=
ervices installed through <strong>AI+ Admin</strong>. So, we will remove a =
lot of containers, images, volumes, and networks and do some system pruning=
.</p>
<p><strong>Important:</strong> If manual removal is not successful, it=E2=
=80=99s <strong>best to create a new user</strong> and perform a fresh inst=
allation. This ensures no residual conflicts, as the installer currently do=
esn=E2=80=99t support upgrades.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"ManualRemovalofAI+Installer-Step-by-StepRemovalInstructions:">Ste=
p-by-Step Removal Instructions:</h3>
<h4 id=3D"ManualRemovalofAI+Installer-1.Stopthepm2process">1. <strong>Stop =
the pm2 process</strong></h4>
<p>Remove AI+ folder and common tool folders:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">pm2 sto=
p all
pm2 delete all</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h4 id=3D"ManualRemovalofAI+Installer-2.Deleteenvironmentandconfigdirectori=
es">2. <strong>Delete environment and config directories</strong></h4>
<p>Remove AI+ folder and common tool folders:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">rm -rf =
~/.aiplus ~/.aws ~/.docker ~/.npm ~/.nvm ~/.pm2</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h4 id=3D"ManualRemovalofAI+Installer-3.StopandremoveallDockercontainers">3=
. <strong>Stop and remove all Docker containers</strong></h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">docker =
stop $(docker ps -aq)
docker rm -f $(docker ps -aq)</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h4 id=3D"ManualRemovalofAI+Installer-4.RemoveDockerimagesandvolumes">4. <s=
trong>Remove Docker images and volumes</strong></h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">docker =
rmi -f $(docker images -q)
docker volume rm $(docker volume ls -q)</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h4 id=3D"ManualRemovalofAI+Installer-5.CleanupDockernetworksandsystemresou=
rces">5. <strong>Clean up Docker networks and system resources</strong></h4=
>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">docker =
network prune -f
docker system prune -a --volumes -f</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h4 id=3D"ManualRemovalofAI+Installer-6.Removecrontabentries(usedtoauthenti=
catedockertoawsECR)"><strong>6. Remove crontab entries (used to authenticat=
e docker to aws ECR)</strong></h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Warni=
ng this is irreversible so all crontab entries will be lost.
# If you don't want that, you can mannually open the crontab entries and ed=
it.
# Remove all crontab entries
crontab -r</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h4 id=3D"ManualRemovalofAI+Installer-7.CheckforactiveservicesonknownAI+por=
ts">7. <strong>Check for active services on known AI+ ports</strong></h4>
<p>AI+ Admin and it=E2=80=99s services runs on ports like:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><code>8080</code> =E2=80=93 Common web apps</p></li>
<li>
<p><code>11434</code> =E2=80=93 Ollama</p></li>
<li>
<p><code>9003</code> =E2=80=93 MetaGen</p></li>
</ul>
<p>Run:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sudo ne=
tstat -tulpn | grep -E '8080|11434|9003'</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h4 id=3D"ManualRemovalofAI+Installer-8.Killprocessesrunningontheseports">8=
. <strong>Kill processes running on these ports</strong></h4>
<p>For each PID returned:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sudo ki=
ll -9 &lt;PID&gt;</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Repeat for <code>11434</code>, <code>9003</code>, etc.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"ManualRemovalofAI+Installer-9.RemoveAuthorizedSSHKeysforFreshInst=
allation">9. Remove Authorized SSH Keys for Fresh Installation</h3>
<p>If you're preparing the system for a <strong>completely fresh installati=
on</strong> under a new or reset user, it's good practice to remove any exi=
sting SSH public keys that may have been used for earlier access.</p>
<p>To remove the existing SSH keys:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">rm ~/.s=
sh/authorized_keys</pre>
</div>
</div>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> This will remove all authorized SSH keys for the =
current user.<br>
If you want to selectively remove keys, open the file using a text editor a=
nd delete the specific lines:</p>
</blockquote>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">nano ~/=
.ssh/authorized_keys</pre>
</div>
</div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
